but difficult to pinpoint where

00:03:10.510 --> 00:03:13.500
exactly it is coming from.

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:17.010
The variable OpEx model of
Cloud with literally thousands

00:03:17.010 --> 00:03:21.050
of cost line items and hundred
more popping every quarter

00:03:21.050 --> 00:03:23.840
doesn't help either.

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:29.380
A common notion we see is that
Cloud cost is not predictable.

00:03:29.380 --> 00:03:31.500
So we need a
framework that is well

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:34.500
understood by finance who
is trying to understand

00:03:34.500 --> 00:03:38.270
the variable OpEx
model, by engineers

00:03:38.270 --> 00:03:41.660
that has to consider
cost as a metric,

00:03:41.660 --> 00:03:45.530
just like reliability and
security of the application,

00:03:45.530 --> 00:03:49.890
and by management that looks at
the value created by the Cloud,

00:03:49.890 --> 00:03:53.150
then just the number
of dollars spent.

00:03:53.150 --> 00:03:55.070
As we discussed
more and more, we

00:03:55.070 --> 00:03:56.900
realized some of
the things we take

00:03:56.900 --> 00:04:00.320
for granted in our experience
